     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Deploying mfa:admin alone prevents exfiltration. Both exfiltration routes need stolen_dbadmin: auth_db and auth_fileserver require it, and escalate_db and escalate_fileserver need it or admin_dc. The only source of stolen_dbadmin is dump_dbadmin_dc, which needs admin_dc. admin_dc comes only from escalate_dc, which needs foothold_dc. foothold_dc comes only from auth_dc, which requires NOT mfa_admin. So with mfa:admin deployed, foothold_dc, admin_dc and stolen_dbadmin are unreachable. That blocks foothold_db, admin_db, foothold_fileserver and admin_fileserver, so exfiltrated can never become true. No smaller set exists, because the attacker wins with zero controls deployed: phish_workstation, pivot_internal, auth_appserver, kerberoast_dc, auth_dc, escalate_dc, dump_dbadmin_dc, auth_db, escalate_db, exfiltrate_db. The minimum is therefore 1.\"}"
    }
